/* Napoli 4–0 Como, 18 May 2031 — fourth successive Scudetto. Five distinct stories with organic supporter threads. */
(()=>{'use strict';const D=window.NAPOLI_DATA||(window.NAPOLI_DATA={});const incoming=[{"id":"napoli-como-four-nil-fourth-scudetto-may18-2031","category":"Serie A","date":"18 May 2031","byline":"Giulia Romano · Radio Napoli Centrale","headline":"QUATTRO. NAPOLI PUT FOUR PAST COMO AND CLAIM A FOURTH CONSECUTIVE SCUDETTO","dek":"Moore scores and creates twice before halftime; Pio, Beier and McTominay complete a 4–0 title-clinching victory at home.","image":"assets/story-napoli-home-crowd.webp","imageCredit":"Season Room · Editorial illustration","longform":true,"body":["The arithmetic had been simple. Beat Como and the championship was Napoli's, whatever happened elsewhere. They answered with a performance nobody will forget. Napoli won 4–0 at home, and for the fourth consecutive season they are champions of Italy.","Mikey Moore scored one and created two before the interval. Pio Esposito and Maximilian Beier finished his passes. Scott McTominay supplied the final goal at 84 minutes. A league title already within reach was seized with both hands.","The first goal arrived at 18 minutes. Estêvão crossed and Moore met it with his head. The young creator had become the finisher, and Napoli had their opening.","At 38, Moore played a beautiful ball to Pio Esposito, who scored. The second goal stretched the advantage and sent the home support another step closer to the celebrations they had waited all season to see.","Five minutes later Moore produced the extraordinary piece of football that defined his afternoon. He spotted Beier's run before it properly developed, played him through alone, and the German finished. Napoli led 3–0. Moore had contributed directly to every goal.","That last assist was not just an accurately struck pass. It was an act of anticipation: identifying the space Beier would attack before the opposition could close it. Beier rewarded the imagination with the finish.","Halftime came with Napoli 3–0 ahead. At Udinese on 10 May, an 87th-minute equaliser from Pafundi had postponed the championship. This time the side had established a cushion that gave Como no comparable opportunity.","The score stayed 3–0 for much of the second half. There is no need to invent chances or incidents to embellish what happened. The three first-half goals had done the most important work.","At 84 minutes Pio delivered a pass to Scott McTominay, and the midfielder scored. Four goals, four different scorers, a clean sheet and, fittingly, a fourth straight Scudetto.","The final whistle raised Napoli to 87 points from 37 Serie A matches: 26 victories, nine draws and two defeats. They have scored 78 league goals and conceded 28, leaving a goal difference of plus fifty.","Inter entered this round with 80 points from 36 matches and therefore could reach at most 86. Roma had 79 from 36 and a maximum of 85. Napoli's 87 points render the results of the chasing clubs irrelevant to the championship. The title is mathematically secured.","This is the fourth consecutive league crown, following 2027–28, 2028–29 and 2029–30. The squad has evolved, the opponents have changed, the pressure has returned every season. Napoli keep finishing first.","The domestic triumph arrives four days after Napoli won the Coppa Italia final 3–1 against Bergamo, with Beier scoring and Pio striking twice. The Supercoppa was won earlier in the campaign. This latest Scudetto gives the club another trophy in a season of immense demands.","Moore finishes the match with a goal and two assists. Pio finishes with a goal and an assist. Beier scores. McTominay scores. Estêvão provides the opening cross. It is the signature of an attack in which the supply comes from everywhere.","The league season still has an away game at AC Milan on 25 May. On 31 May Napoli face Paris Saint-Germain in their fourth consecutive Champions League final, chasing a third successive European title. Neither future match has been played.","Those are questions for another day. This night belongs to the players, supporters and a championship won without favours from anyone. Napoli needed a victory. They gave their city four goals.","Four consecutive Scudetti. Napoli are champions again."],"comments":[{"user":"CurvaB","text":"QUATTRO SCUDETTI CONSECUTIVI. SAY IT UNTIL THE WINDOWS SHAKE.","replies":[{"user":"NapoliTherapy","text":"My entire building started shouting at the fourth. Even the old man upstairs who usually complains about noise.","replies":[{"user":"CurvaB","text":"HE HAS FINALLY SEEN THE LIGHT.","replies":[]}]},{"user":"OldSchoolNapoli","text":"The man upstairs probably remembers how long it took us to win just one.","replies":[{"user":"CurvaB","text":"THEN HE CAN LEAD THE NEXT SONG","replies":[]}]}]},{"user":"MooreMagic","text":"A goal and TWO assists before halftime. THE MIKEY MOORE SHOW.","replies":[{"user":"TacticalNonno","text":"The pass at 43 beat the defender before Beier even reached the space.","replies":[{"user":"MooreMagic","text":"Exactly. I watched it again and shouted at the screen.","replies":[]}]},{"user":"BeierHive","text":"And Beier committed to that run without looking over his shoulder. Both trusted the other.","replies":[]}]},{"user":"PioNation","text":"45 GOALS AND AN ASSIST FOR SCOTT. HE IS EVERYWHERE.","replies":[{"user":"PioHaterForNoReason","text":"One goal in a four-goal win. Concerning.","replies":[{"user":"PioNation","text":"PLEASE NOT TONIGHT","replies":[{"user":"PioHaterForNoReason","text":"I waited until the title was mathematically certain. That is restraint.","replies":[]}]}]},{"user":"McTominayEngine","text":"He also spotted Scott's run at 84. I'd happily take that sort of selfishness.","replies":[{"user":"PioNation","text":"Exactly why I said he's everywhere.","replies":[]}]}]},{"user":"BeierHive","text":"The pass arrives and Beier is gone. They make a difficult action look automatic.","replies":[]},{"user":"NapoliDoomer","text":"I spent the entire second half waiting to be hurt again after Udinese.","replies":[{"user":"NapoliTherapy","text":"Udinese did that to all of us. Three nil and I was still checking the clock.","replies":[{"user":"NapoliDoomer","text":"I checked it after Scott scored too. Completely irrational.","replies":[]}]},{"user":"OldSchoolNapoli","text":"Title races leave bruises. Winning one doesn't immediately take them away.","replies":[]}]},{"user":"TacticalNonno","text":"Header, pass to Pio, early ball to Beier. Moore defeated the same defence three different ways.","replies":[{"user":"PazAppreciation","text":"Three answers to three different questions","replies":[]}]},{"user":"SaladinoOutNow","text":"Four titles and the manager still can't arrange five goals against Como. Complacency.","replies":[{"user":"CurvaB","text":"NAME A SINGLE RESULT THAT WOULD SATISFY YOU.","replies":[{"user":"SaladinoOutNow","text":"Five goals in a four-goal win would have been a start.","replies":[]}]},{"user":"NapoliTherapy","text":"He's going to show up at the parade with a protest placard.","replies":[{"user":"SaladinoOutNow","text":"My placard says WHERE IS NUMBER FIVE?","replies":[]}]}]},{"user":"InterNorth","text":"An Inter supporter saying congratulations. No excuse remains after 87 points.","replies":[{"user":"CurvaB","text":"Respect for coming here after a long chase.","replies":[{"user":"InterNorth","text":"I can dislike Napoli and still recognise that 87 points is a champion's work.","replies":[]}]},{"user":"RomaObserver","text":"We came after the same title, and today settled it for both of us.","replies":[]}]},{"user":"RomaObserver","text":"Roma were in this title race too. In the end Napoli won it emphatically. Four straight championships deserves respect.","replies":[]},{"user":"OldSchoolNapoli","text":"There were years when a single title seemed impossible. Four consecutive is difficult to describe.","replies":[{"user":"AzzurriSouth","text":"Never forget how exceptional this is","replies":[]}]},{"user":"McTominayEngine","text":"SCOTT IN THE 84TH. I COULDN'T HAVE WRITTEN IT BETTER.","replies":[{"user":"StachAppreciation","text":"That is why you watch all those runs he makes when nobody passes to him. Sometimes he gets the reward.","replies":[{"user":"McTominayEngine","text":"And the moment happened on the day the league was decided.","replies":[]}]},{"user":"PioNation","text":"Loved the pass to him. Pio didn't just turn up to score his 45th.","replies":[]}]},{"user":"EstevaoElectric","text":"The cross to Moore at 18 started everything. Don't lose Estêvão in the headlines.","replies":[]},{"user":"CurvaCalculator","text":"87 points. Inter's maximum was 86 and Roma's was 85. I'm finally closing the calculator app.","replies":[{"user":"ScudettoWatch","text":"Finally I can delete the permutations","replies":[]}]},{"user":"KvaraMemories","text":"From losing to PSG in 2028 to four consecutive league titles. What a journey.","replies":[{"user":"OldSchoolNapoli","text":"The loss to PSG in 2028 is still part of this story. It makes days like today even sweeter.","replies":[{"user":"KvaraMemories","text":"And we get to meet them again with the Scudetto in our hands.","replies":[]}]},{"user":"ParisObserver","text":"Enjoy your afternoon. Our final will have its own ending.","replies":[]}]},{"user":"NapoliTherapy","text":"I actually laughed at the fourth goal. The title was finally beyond nerves.","replies":[{"user":"NapoliDoomer","text":"Pafundi had me convinced the entire universe was against us.","replies":[{"user":"NapoliTherapy","text":"Even at four nil?","replies":[{"user":"NapoliDoomer","text":"I still checked for an offside flag.","replies":[]}]}]}]},{"user":"BuongiornoWall","text":"FOUR GOALS AND A CLEAN SHEET. The second part is beautiful too.","replies":[]},{"user":"AzzurriSouth","text":"POSSEDIAMO L'ITALIAAAAAA.","replies":[{"user":"CurvaB","text":"AND NOW THE WHOLE CITY KNOWS","replies":[]}]},{"user":"ScudettoWatch","text":"Cup won four days ago. League won today. Supercoppa already won. This season has been serious.","replies":[{"user":"PioNation","text":"And the biggest European night still awaits","replies":[]}]},{"user":"PazAppreciation","text":"Paz, Moore, Estêvão, Olise, Neves. So many routes into the forwards.","replies":[{"user":"TacticalNonno","text":"The hardest teams to stop have three ways to build the same chance. We've got more than three.","replies":[{"user":"PazAppreciation","text":"Exactly why giving everyone a role is more useful than picking one saviour.","replies":[]}]},{"user":"BeierHive","text":"And Beier gets to make those runs while the defender is busy counting creators.","replies":[]}]},{"user":"OliseAppreciation","text":"Olise supplied the opening goal in the cup final. He's a big part of the reason we can celebrate both trophies this week.","replies":[{"user":"OldSchoolNapoli","text":"Especially those whose futures are changing","replies":[]}]},{"user":"BergamoVisitor","text":"Napoli beat us in the cup and followed it with this. Fair play.","replies":[]},{"user":"ParisObserver","text":"Congratulations Napoli. We'll see you on May 31.","replies":[{"user":"KvaraMemories","text":"Neither of us is forgetting 2028. That is precisely why the rematch matters.","replies":[{"user":"ParisObserver","text":"Agreed, and we'll come to play our own game.","replies":[]}]},{"user":"CurvaB","text":"I AM TAKING TONIGHT OFF FROM EUROPEAN PANIC.","replies":[]}]},{"user":"MooreMagic","text":"If that assist for Beier was a painting I would hang it in my kitchen.","replies":[{"user":"NapoliTherapy","text":"Your kitchen has no more wall space","replies":[]}]},{"user":"RossettiWatch","text":"The young players are growing up inside a title-winning culture.","replies":[]},{"user":"StachAppreciation","text":"McT on the scoresheet, Stach had his cup moment, and every unglamorous minute mattered.","replies":[{"user":"McTominayEngine","text":"Champions are built from those minutes","replies":[]}]},{"user":"PioHaterForNoReason","text":"Only 45 goals this season. Surely the minimum is 46.","replies":[{"user":"PioNation","text":"He can score number 46 in Milan. Tonight he deserves a plate of pasta and peace.","replies":[{"user":"PioHaterForNoReason","text":"I shall be watching his fork technique.","replies":[]}]}]},{"user":"NapoliDoomer","text":"Can we take one night off from worrying about PSG?","replies":[{"user":"NapoliTherapy","text":"You have until May 31 to ruin your sleep. Enjoy a single evening.","replies":[{"user":"NapoliDoomer","text":"I already have a reminder telling me to stop checking the calendar.","replies":[]}]}]},{"user":"AzzurriSouth","text":"Four goals, four scorers, four Scudetti. A number with a certain poetry to it.","replies":[{"user":"CurvaB","text":"POETRY IN BLUE","replies":[]}]},{"user":"PeacockUnion","text":"The team kept Como out while the forwards had their party. Lovely.","replies":[]},{"user":"CurvaB","text":"THIS IS WHY WE NEVER STOP SINGING.","replies":[{"user":"OldSchoolNapoli","text":"Don't stop singing. But some of us have work in the morning.","replies":[{"user":"CurvaB","text":"GOOD LUCK FINDING A QUIET STREET TOMORROW.","replies":[]}]},{"user":"AzzurriSouth","text":"STASERA NUN SE DORME!","replies":[]}]},{"user":"ViaToledo","text":"I took my father out onto the street when the whistle went. He stood under the flags saying 'four' as if he still couldn't believe it.","replies":[{"user":"OldSchoolNapoli","text":"Some of us spent decades hoping for just one. Give him all the time he needs.","replies":[{"user":"ViaToledo","text":"I think I finally understood what all those stories he told me meant.","replies":[]}]},{"user":"CurvaB","text":"BRING HIM TO THE PARADE. HE CAN STAND WITH US.","replies":[]}]},{"user":"SouthStand93","text":"Everyone's talking about the ball at 43. The pass to Pio at 38 was beautiful as well. Five minutes apart, two completely different decisions.","replies":[{"user":"PioNation","text":"Thank you! It was already two nil because Moore saw Pio in the right place.","replies":[]},{"user":"MooreMagic","text":"I have replayed both so many times I'm seeing them when I blink.","replies":[]}]},{"user":"InterNorth","text":"I had begun believing again when Udinese equalised. Then Moore destroyed that belief before halftime today.","replies":[{"user":"RomaObserver","text":"You're not alone. We were waiting for something to reopen the race.","replies":[{"user":"InterNorth","text":"Three goals in forty-three minutes. Hard to argue with that.","replies":[]}]}]},{"user":"BeierHive","text":"Watch the third goal again. Beier starts his run before Moore actually passes. He knows the ball is coming.","replies":[{"user":"TacticalNonno","text":"That's chemistry, not clairvoyance. But it looks like clairvoyance when both get the timing right.","replies":[]},{"user":"MooreMagic","text":"I choose to believe they communicated telepathically.","replies":[]}]},{"user":"NapoliTherapy","text":"There will be a lot of people calling in sick tomorrow. Nobody is sleeping tonight.","replies":[{"user":"ViaToledo","text":"My family has already decided the celebrations continue over breakfast.","replies":[]},{"user":"NapoliDoomer","text":"I took tomorrow off in case we LOST. I am delighted to have been wrong.","replies":[]}]},{"user":"StachAppreciation","text":"A title has more authors than the lads who appear in the scoring column. Think of every grim away fixture we survived.","replies":[{"user":"OldSchoolNapoli","text":"Exactly. Players who got us through the hard matches won't fit into one headline.","replies":[{"user":"McTominayEngine","text":"And it's lovely that Scott got his moment on this night.","replies":[]}]}]},{"user":"CurvaB","text":"THE TROPHY ISN'T EVEN COOL YET AND MY UNCLE ALREADY BOUGHT A FLAG WITH FOUR ON IT.","replies":[{"user":"AzzurriSouth","text":"MIO ZIO HA APPESO LA BANDIERA DAL BALCONE!","replies":[{"user":"CurvaB","text":"A GREAT FAMILY OF EDUCATED MEN.","replies":[]}]}]},{"user":"RossettiWatch","text":"If you're a young player at this club, you watched Moore help decide a championship today. That is the standard in front of you.","replies":[{"user":"TacticalNonno","text":"And you watched McTominay contribute after years of hard work. The other half of the lesson.","replies":[]}]},{"user":"KvaraMemories","text":"A title is for the people who stuck through everything. I keep thinking of friends who aren't here to see number four.","replies":[{"user":"OldSchoolNapoli","text":"That hits harder than any trophy photograph. Forza Napoli, for all of them.","replies":[]}]},{"user":"PazAppreciation","text":"Moore gets tonight's headlines, but Paz deserves to be part of this week's celebration too. Remember the Coppa final.","replies":[{"user":"MooreMagic","text":"Absolutely. Having several players capable of deciding games is the whole point.","replies":[]}]},{"user":"McTominayEngine","text":"I cheered more for Scott's fourth than for any of the other goals. That says something about how much the workhorse means to us.","replies":[{"user":"PioNation","text":"Pio saw his run perfectly. The last goal was a little reward for everyone.","replies":[]},{"user":"OldSchoolNapoli","text":"A workhorse scoring on title day is the right kind of football story.","replies":[]}]},{"user":"NapoliDoomer","text":"I genuinely thought the league would still find a way to go wrong at three nil. I need professional assistance.","replies":[{"user":"NapoliTherapy","text":"The professional assistance is a large plate of pasta and turning the phone off.","replies":[{"user":"NapoliDoomer","text":"I can do the pasta. I can't do the phone.","replies":[]}]}]},{"user":"CurvaB","text":"IF ANYONE NEEDS ME I WILL BE OUT THE WINDOW SHOUTING QUATTRO AT EVERY PASSERBY.","replies":[{"user":"OldSchoolNapoli","text":"Be kind to the people trying to get home.","replies":[{"user":"CurvaB","text":"THEY MAY COME IN FOR PASTA.","replies":[]}]}]}]},{"id":"moore-como-goal-two-assists-title-may18-2031","category":"Player Focus","date":"19 May 2031","byline":"Elena De Luca · Player Desk","headline":"MIKEY MOORE SAW THE RUN BEFORE BEIER MADE IT","dek":"The winger's headed opener, pass to Pio and brilliant ball to Beier gave Napoli three first-half goals and the Scudetto.","image":"assets/story-sandro-player-guidance.webp","imageCredit":"Season Room · Editorial illustration","longform":true,"body":["Three contributions in 43 minutes. One headed goal and two assists. Mikey Moore's title-clinching performance against Como was the sort of display that makes a player's reputation change in a single afternoon.","Napoli needed a win to secure their fourth consecutive Scudetto. The young winger gave them an early lead, widened it through his passing and then delivered the outstanding moment of the game.","At 18 minutes, he met Estêvão's cross with his head. It was a scorer's movement, not the obvious outcome for a player more often admired for invention out wide.","At 38 minutes he found Pio Esposito with a beautiful pass. The striker finished, collecting his 45th competitive Napoli goal of the season.","At 43 Moore noticed Beier's attacking run before the movement had completely taken shape. He slipped the ball into the space the German was about to occupy. Beier went through alone and scored for 3–0.","To describe that last pass as vision is accurate but incomplete. Vision tells a footballer where another player is. Moore's decision seemed to depend on understanding where Beier would be a moment later.","The move demanded trust in both directions. Moore trusted the run; Beier trusted that the ball would arrive. The finish completed a conversation the two players had conducted without a word.","The range is striking. A header from Estêvão's cross, a combination with Pio and a perfectly timed through ball for Beier. Each threatened Como differently.","This was not Moore's only decisive contribution to the league run-in. At Sassuolo on 4 May he assisted Olise's volley and then scored from a Beier pass. The title race was still open then.","Now his Napoli competitive-season figures stand at ten goals and thirteen assists. His Napoli club-career totals rise to seventeen goals and twenty-eight assists. That is substantial production from a young player still developing his game.","It would be misleading to call the night a solo victory. Estêvão provided his opener. Pio and Beier finished the assists. McTominay made it four in the 84th minute after another Pio pass. Moore had outstanding teammates, and he used them.","But neither should the individual achievement disappear beneath a generic celebration of teamwork. When the title depended on this game, Moore shaped the first half of it.","The player is still learning. There will be passes that do not find their target and matches where invention requires patience. Nothing about a championship erases development.","What the afternoon established is that imagination can survive pressure. Some players retreat into conservative choices when the consequences become enormous. Moore chose the audacious pass that broke open a title decider.","The fourth Scudetto belongs to Napoli's entire season. The first half against Como belongs, unmistakably, to Mikey Moore."],"comments":[{"user":"MooreMagic","text":"THE THIRD GOAL. THAT PASS. I AM GOING TO TALK ABOUT IT FOREVER.","replies":[{"user":"BeierHive","text":"Beier started running without even checking if Moore could find him.","replies":[{"user":"MooreMagic","text":"And the pass arrived exactly where he'd committed to be.","replies":[]}]},{"user":"TacticalNonno","text":"Watch the defender. He cannot step towards Moore and cover the run at the same time. That's what the timing creates.","replies":[]}]},{"user":"TacticalNonno","text":"The timing is more impressive than the distance. Early passes make defenders look slow.","replies":[{"user":"OldSchoolNapoli","text":"A proper football observation","replies":[]}]},{"user":"PioNation","text":"Moore's ball for Pio was beautiful too. Don't let the third erase the second.","replies":[{"user":"MooreMagic","text":"Everybody's going on about 43, but I loved the decision at 38 as well. No need to force the shot.","replies":[{"user":"PioNation","text":"Exactly, and Pio still had to finish it.","replies":[]}]},{"user":"TacticalNonno","text":"Two different passes, each correct for a different movement.","replies":[]}]},{"user":"EstevaoElectric","text":"He scored a header from Estêvão's cross. The creator became the finisher.","replies":[{"user":"OliseAppreciation","text":"The attack has no fixed direction","replies":[]}]},{"user":"NapoliTherapy","text":"I wasn't prepared for the header, then I wasn't prepared for the passes.","replies":[]},{"user":"BeierHive","text":"An early pass is useless if the runner doesn't understand it. Give both their flowers.","replies":[{"user":"MooreMagic","text":"If Beier waits for Moore to lift his head, the opportunity's gone.","replies":[{"user":"BeierHive","text":"Which is why he doesn't wait. He trusts the ball will arrive.","replies":[]}]},{"user":"PazAppreciation","text":"That trust is easier to see after a few months of watching them combine.","replies":[]}]},{"user":"CurvaB","text":"Ten goals and thirteen assists. He's a lot more than a promising winger now.","replies":[]},{"user":"PioHaterForNoReason","text":"Moore should have scored all four himself. Excessive generosity.","replies":[{"user":"PioNation","text":"HELP IS AVAILABLE","replies":[]}]},{"user":"PazAppreciation","text":"Please don't turn Moore's performance into a made-up rivalry with Paz.","replies":[{"user":"TacticalNonno","text":"Paz and Moore solve different problems. There will be games for both approaches.","replies":[{"user":"PazAppreciation","text":"Exactly. I'd rather have two answers than an argument about whose name is bigger.","replies":[]}]}]},{"user":"InterNorth","text":"That pass for Beier was fantastic, even viewed through an Inter fan's pain.","replies":[{"user":"CurvaB","text":"IF EVEN AN INTER FAN ADMITS IT, IT MUST HAVE BEEN BEAUTIFUL.","replies":[{"user":"InterNorth","text":"Do not expect a second compliment. I've already suffered enough.","replies":[]}]}]},{"user":"RossettiWatch","text":"The developmental point matters. A spectacular title game doesn't mean the kid has nothing left to learn.","replies":[]},{"user":"McTominayEngine","text":"Moore controlled the first half, Scott marked the finish. Everyone has a part.","replies":[]},{"user":"KvaraMemories","text":"Let this winger become his own player. No need to measure him against every previous Napoli star.","replies":[]},{"user":"AzzurriSouth","text":"QUEL PASSAGGIO PER BEIER. MAMMA MIA.","replies":[{"user":"CurvaB","text":"ARTE","replies":[]}]},{"user":"SaladinoOutNow","text":"Ten goals and thirteen assists suggests indecision. Is he a scorer or a provider?","replies":[{"user":"TacticalNonno","text":"The kid has ten goals and thirteen assists. That is a complete attacker, not an indecisive one.","replies":[{"user":"SaladinoOutNow","text":"I am worried about him being too complete. Where is the room for improvement?","replies":[]}]},{"user":"MooreMagic","text":"Your argument has somehow become that he's too good.","replies":[]}]},{"user":"MooreMagic","text":"He didn't just pick out Beier. He knew the run would appear.","replies":[{"user":"BeierHive","text":"That is what makes it extraordinary","replies":[]}]},{"user":"BuongiornoWall","text":"Creativity matters. Doing it in the decisive match matters more.","replies":[]},{"user":"PioNation","text":"Pio is on 45 goals because his teammates actually see the runs.","replies":[]},{"user":"ParisObserver","text":"That is the kind of through ball a European opponent must prepare for.","replies":[{"user":"BeierHive","text":"And a runner who can finish it","replies":[]}]},{"user":"OliseAppreciation","text":"Competition for creative roles is a good football problem, not a tabloid crisis.","replies":[]},{"user":"NapoliDoomer","text":"I was afraid to enjoy the 3–0 because of Udinese, which is ridiculous.","replies":[{"user":"NapoliTherapy","text":"I know. Pafundi ruined my ability to enjoy a lead.","replies":[{"user":"NapoliDoomer","text":"Even when we made it three I kept looking at the clock.","replies":[{"user":"NapoliTherapy","text":"And Scott finally made it four. Please tell me you relaxed then.","replies":[]}]}]}]},{"user":"PeacockUnion","text":"The best attacking support for a clean sheet is four goals at the other end.","replies":[{"user":"BuongiornoWall","text":"Still takes discipline","replies":[]}]},{"user":"ScudettoWatch","text":"Sassuolo showed this wasn't just one magic afternoon. The kid had already been decisive in a title run-in.","replies":[]},{"user":"OldSchoolNapoli","text":"He'll play tougher opponents, but no one can take this contribution away.","replies":[{"user":"CurvaB","text":"WE WILL REMEMBER THIS","replies":[]}]},{"user":"StachAppreciation","text":"That move requires the striker to sprint knowing a pass may never arrive.","replies":[{"user":"BeierHive","text":"He had to take the chance that the pass might never come.","replies":[{"user":"StachAppreciation","text":"That's the part casual viewers miss. The run is a decision too.","replies":[]}]}]},{"user":"MooreMagic","text":"Watch the pass to Pio and you'll see the same instinct expressed differently.","replies":[{"user":"PioNation","text":"Yes. Different finish, same quality","replies":[]}]},{"user":"AzzurriSouth","text":"GIOVANE E CORAGGIOSO. This is how you play for Napoli.","replies":[{"user":"CurvaB","text":"WITH YOUR HEART","replies":[]}]},{"user":"RomaObserver","text":"A neutralish observer: his performance made the title decider surprisingly one-sided.","replies":[]},{"user":"NapoliTherapy","text":"The header at 18 is being buried under the passes. The movement to meet Estêvão's cross deserves some credit.","replies":[{"user":"MooreMagic","text":"That is the most poetic thing you've posted","replies":[]}]},{"user":"CurvaB","text":"I WANT A STATUE OF THE PASS. NOT THE PLAYER. THE PASS.","replies":[{"user":"TacticalNonno","text":"You'd be sculpting an empty channel in the grass.","replies":[{"user":"CurvaB","text":"THEN THAT'S WHERE WE PUT THE STATUE.","replies":[]}]},{"user":"BeierHive","text":"Please leave enough room for Maxi to sprint through it.","replies":[]}]},{"user":"SouthStand93","text":"Moore's ball to Pio is going to get ignored because of the Beier assist. That's a shame. It was the right pass at the right moment.","replies":[{"user":"PioNation","text":"Thank you. Pio didn't get to 45 by finishing passes that never arrive.","replies":[]},{"user":"MooreMagic","text":"I've watched both goals again. You can praise one without taking anything from the other.","replies":[]}]}]},{"id":"napoli-four-straight-scudetti-dynasty-may19-2031","category":"Club History","date":"19 May 2031","byline":"Marco Bellini · Il Calcio Sera","headline":"FOUR YEARS AT THE SUMMIT. NAPOLI HAVE MADE THE EXCEPTIONAL ROUTINE.","dek":"87 points, four consecutive Scudetti and a changing squad that has learned how to keep winning under pressure.","image":"assets/story-naples-vesuvius-sunset.webp","imageCredit":"Season Room · Editorial illustration","longform":true,"body":["A Scudetto confirms a season. Four consecutive Scudetti define an era. Napoli have made themselves champions of Italy again by beating Como 4–0, moving to 87 points with one league match still to play.","The title seasons now form an uninterrupted sequence: 2027–28, 2028–29, 2029–30, 2030–31. The fifth remains a future ambition, not a present claim. Four are real.","The decisive afternoon offered a compact illustration of the team's evolution. Estêvão supplied a cross for Moore's header. Moore played Pio in for the second, then anticipated Beier's run for the third. Pio created the fourth for McTominay.","The attacking responsibilities are shared even in a side with extraordinary individual totals. Pio now has 45 competitive Napoli goals and 19 assists this season. Beier has 41 and 35. Moore has reached ten and thirteen. There are different kinds of influence behind the same silverware.","The defence is part of that story. Napoli have scored 78 goals in 37 Serie A fixtures and conceded 28. A goal difference of plus fifty does not belong to an attack alone.","The championship has not been achieved by reliving a single winning lineup. Players have arrived, others have moved on or prepared to depart, and experienced footballers have made room for younger ones. The standard has endured changes in personnel.","There have been difficult episodes. Torino beat Napoli in April. Udinese's late equaliser in May delayed a celebration. The league title was still technically open when Napoli approached Como.","What followed those disappointments matters more than the notion of never suffering them: Napoli won the Coppa Italia final against Bergamo on 14 May, then returned home to take the Serie A title four days later.","The Supercoppa was won earlier this season. The domestic collection is already a formidable achievement. There is no need to turn the unplayed Champions League final into another completed success.","European history provides both joy and motivation. Paris Saint-Germain beat Napoli in the 2028 final. The following seasons brought victories over Real Madrid in 2029 and Porto in 2030. On 31 May PSG will be the opponent again, in Napoli's fourth consecutive Champions League final.","Even a result there cannot change the domestic record established here. Four consecutive Italian championships represent consistency at the highest national level, not simply a collection of spectacular matchdays.","For the supporters who lived through seasons when even one championship looked remote, the accumulation is almost difficult to process. For those growing up during these years, the club's challenge is not to allow achievement to become entitlement.","The league season ends with a visit to AC Milan on 25 May. There will be decisions about how to play it before the European final. Those decisions belong to football's future, not the fact of what has just been won.","In the record books the score is simple: Napoli 4–0 Como, 18 May 2031. Underneath it sits a far bigger story. Napoli have become a club capable of doing the exceptional four times in succession.","The title is no longer a hope. It is a standard this generation has established."],"comments":[{"user":"OldSchoolNapoli","text":"Four consecutive titles. I never imagined we'd be discussing them in the plural like this.","replies":[{"user":"CurvaB","text":"MY GRANDFATHER TOLD ME NEVER TO TAKE EVEN ONE TITLE FOR GRANTED.","replies":[{"user":"OldSchoolNapoli","text":"Your grandfather is correct. I'm old enough to remember why.","replies":[]}]},{"user":"KvaraMemories","text":"Every hard year is part of the story. The people who were there for those will never say winning is routine.","replies":[]}]},{"user":"ScudettoWatch","text":"2027–28. 2028–29. 2029–30. 2030–31. I wrote the years down and they still don't quite look real.","replies":[]},{"user":"KvaraMemories","text":"Include the PSG loss in 2028. A dynasty is built partly by responding to defeats.","replies":[{"user":"ParisObserver","text":"We remember that final too. But these teams aren't the same as in 2028.","replies":[{"user":"KvaraMemories","text":"Exactly. History matters without being a prediction.","replies":[]}]},{"user":"OldSchoolNapoli","text":"Two European titles followed that defeat. That's the kind of answer I admire.","replies":[]}]},{"user":"TacticalNonno","text":"Adaptation is the most important word. Opponents change; the team finds new solutions.","replies":[{"user":"PazAppreciation","text":"Look at how many different players supplied goals in the Coppa and then Como.","replies":[{"user":"TacticalNonno","text":"And that comes from the ability to change shape while keeping the same attacking principles.","replies":[]}]},{"user":"BeierHive","text":"It helps Beier be a creator as often as he is a scorer.","replies":[]}]},{"user":"NapoliTherapy","text":"People born during the first title are about to take winning the league for granted.","replies":[{"user":"OldSchoolNapoli","text":"Their parents must teach them otherwise","replies":[]}]},{"user":"CurvaB","text":"DYNASTY IN BLUE. IF YOU HAVE A PROBLEM WITH THE WORD, COUNT THE CUPS.","replies":[{"user":"SaladinoOutNow","text":"Still no fifth consecutive title. Why stop now?","replies":[{"user":"CurvaB","text":"BECAUSE THERE ISN'T A FIFTH SEASON YET.","replies":[{"user":"SaladinoOutNow","text":"A truly ambitious manager would have planned around that.","replies":[]}]}]}]},{"user":"InterNorth","text":"Inter chased hard. Napoli earned the league. Congratulations.","replies":[{"user":"RomaObserver","text":"Roma tried as well, but 87 ended it","replies":[]}]},{"user":"PioNation","text":"Pio 45 and 19. I need a bigger notebook.","replies":[{"user":"BeierHive","text":"Forty-one goals and thirty-five assists. I won't turn this into a contest between two forwards tonight.","replies":[{"user":"PioNation","text":"Good, because forty-five and nineteen makes a fine partnership.","replies":[]}]},{"user":"OldSchoolNapoli","text":"And four different scorers sealed the title. That matters too.","replies":[]}]},{"user":"BeierHive","text":"No dynasty article is complete without what Beier has become as a creator.","replies":[{"user":"TacticalNonno","text":"That is a defining tactical change","replies":[]}]},{"user":"MooreMagic","text":"Young fans will think one goal and two assists in title deciders is normal.","replies":[]},{"user":"BergamoVisitor","text":"Losing to them in the cup and seeing this league performance makes the level clear.","replies":[]},{"user":"NapoliDoomer","text":"Four years of winning has not cured my anxiety. How is that possible?","replies":[{"user":"NapoliTherapy","text":"It has become part of your identity","replies":[]}]},{"user":"RossettiWatch","text":"Four titles is a massive foundation for the next generation.","replies":[]},{"user":"PazAppreciation","text":"The next question is how you keep everyone hungry when even the younger players are used to trophies. That's a challenge worth having.","replies":[{"user":"TacticalNonno","text":"Depth does not require drama","replies":[]}]},{"user":"PeacockUnion","text":"78 scored, 28 conceded. This achievement has two sides of the ball.","replies":[]},{"user":"CurvaCalculator","text":"26 wins, nine draws, two defeats. Not a flawless season, but an incredibly relentless one.","replies":[{"user":"ScudettoWatch","text":"An impressive season, documented cleanly","replies":[]}]},{"user":"OliseAppreciation","text":"Olise deserves his share of the credit before the summer changes the squad.","replies":[{"user":"KvaraMemories","text":"Olise's cross in the cup final is as much part of this week as any Como moment.","replies":[{"user":"OliseAppreciation","text":"And he still wears our shirt. Let's appreciate what remains instead of talking about him in the past tense.","replies":[]}]}]},{"user":"RomaObserver","text":"You can't dismiss four straight titles as luck. No serious supporter should.","replies":[{"user":"InterNorth","text":"Uncomfortable agreement","replies":[]}]},{"user":"SaladinoOutNow","text":"I will acknowledge the dynasty once it reaches six consecutive titles.","replies":[]},{"user":"NapoliTherapy","text":"Udinese felt like disaster. Como made it look like a footnote.","replies":[{"user":"NapoliDoomer","text":"I would like the footnote erased","replies":[]}]},{"user":"McTominayEngine","text":"A midfield workhorse scores the fourth. Nice symbolism.","replies":[{"user":"StachAppreciation","text":"A whole squad's trophy","replies":[]}]},{"user":"KvaraMemories","text":"2028 Paris hurt. Madrid and Porto healed much of it. What a story.","replies":[{"user":"ParisObserver","text":"Our meeting in 2028 changed both teams in different ways.","replies":[{"user":"KvaraMemories","text":"It changed how I watch finals. I won't pretend otherwise.","replies":[]}]}]},{"user":"AzzurriSouth","text":"QUATTRO ANNI. QUATTRO SCUDETTI. NAPOLI PER SEMPRE.","replies":[]},{"user":"EstevaoElectric","text":"The next generation is already contributing, not just waiting in line.","replies":[{"user":"RossettiWatch","text":"Exactly what continuity should look like","replies":[]}]},{"user":"BuongiornoWall","text":"The clean-sheet side of the title winner isn't glamorous but it's essential.","replies":[]},{"user":"CurvaB","text":"I AM NEVER GOING TO SAY 'JUST A LEAGUE TITLE'.","replies":[]},{"user":"ScudettoWatch","text":"Milan away still matters for finishing well, even with the trophy decided.","replies":[{"user":"NapoliTherapy","text":"I am granting myself one night without calculations","replies":[]}]},{"user":"PioHaterForNoReason","text":"A dynasty with no grounds for complaint is the greatest problem of all.","replies":[{"user":"PioNation","text":"YOU HAVE FOUND MANY GROUNDS ANYWAY","replies":[]}]},{"user":"AzzurriSouth","text":"L'ITALIA È AZZURRA.","replies":[{"user":"CurvaB","text":"E RESTA AZZURRA","replies":[]}]}]},{"id":"bellandi-scudetto-paris-not-yet-may19-2031","category":"Opinion","date":"19 May 2031","byline":"Matteo Bellandi · Linea Calcio","headline":"BELLANDI: FOUR SCUDETTI ARE NO ACCIDENT. PARIS IS STILL A DIFFERENT QUESTION.","dek":"A skeptical pundit gives Napoli their due after Como, and refuses to call the Champions League final before it is played.","image":"assets/story-touchline-pressure.webp","imageCredit":"Season Room · Editorial illustration","longform":true,"body":["I've criticised Napoli when they deserved criticism. I've asked questions after dropped points, late concessions and moments of hesitation. After the 4–0 win against Como, there is a simpler question: what exactly is left to debate about the Serie A champion?","Four consecutive Scudetti. Twenty-six wins, nine draws and two defeats this season, with one league match still outstanding. Eighty-seven points, a total neither Inter nor Roma can reach.","It did not happen because the chasers suddenly stopped competing. It happened because Napoli kept doing enough across the full campaign to remain above them.","The Como game was almost offensively decisive. Moore headed in Estêvão's cross at 18 minutes, sent Pio through at 38 and read Beier's run to perfection at 43. Three goals before the interval, a title all but settled.","Pio then assisted McTominay's goal at 84. It was the right kind of exclamation mark: a midfielder whose work is often judged by the things he prevents rather than the things he scores.","Moore was the outstanding performer, but nobody should turn that into a competition between him and the other creative players. The forwards finished his passes. Estêvão created his goal. A superb team performance contains distinct individual contributions.","The 1–1 draw at Udinese on 10 May was a real warning about how a title chase can be prolonged. It is not suddenly foolish to remember that Pafundi equalised in the 87th minute. Champions can have weak moments and still deserve their championship.","Napoli answered by beating Bergamo 3–1 in the Coppa Italia final and then dismantling Como. If you want the response to a late setback, look at those two results.","There is a temptation to interpret the fourth Scudetto as an advance guarantee of the Champions League. Do not do it. PSG will not concede three goals because Napoli scored three before halftime against Como.","The 2028 final went Paris's way, 3–2 after extra time. Napoli won the next two European finals against Real Madrid and Porto. Now PSG are waiting again on 31 May, and Napoli are chasing a third consecutive European crown.","That is a magnificent story. It is also an unfinished one. Football does not reward historical momentum with a goal before kickoff.","Before Paris comes the league finale at AC Milan. The title cannot be lost there, but maintaining rhythm and choosing the right players will still matter. Intelligent rotation should be judged by its consequences, not treated as betrayal.","I know what some fans will say: that a man who has questioned this side should now apologise for ever asking anything. That is not analysis. Good teams need honest questions, and great teams earn honest praise.","Napoli have earned it. A fourth Scudetto in succession deserves admiration without qualification. The coming European final deserves anticipation without certainty.","Celebrate the title. Then let Paris write its own ending."],"comments":[{"user":"CurvaB","text":"BELLANDI PRAISING US ON TITLE NIGHT. I HAVE SEEN EVERYTHING.","replies":[{"user":"NapoliTherapy","text":"He spent last week talking about how we would crack under pressure. Tonight he's praising them.","replies":[{"user":"CurvaB","text":"IT'S CALLED A BEAUTIFUL EDUCATION.","replies":[]}]},{"user":"TacticalNonno","text":"He still thinks the Udinese draw was a warning. That's not inherently inconsistent with praising a champion.","replies":[]}]},{"user":"SaladinoOutNow","text":"Bellandi has abandoned scrutiny. Only four league titles!","replies":[{"user":"TacticalNonno","text":"How exactly is the manager supposed to have won next season's league already?","replies":[{"user":"SaladinoOutNow","text":"A good manager would have made arrangements.","replies":[]}]},{"user":"CurvaB","text":"YOU'LL BE PROTESTING AT THE PARADE, WON'T YOU?","replies":[{"user":"SaladinoOutNow","text":"I own a portable charger. I can continue all day.","replies":[]}]}]},{"user":"TacticalNonno","text":"He's right that Paris is a different match, but I don't agree that Milan away is only about preserving legs. Rhythm matters too.","replies":[{"user":"ParisObserver","text":"We agree on that","replies":[]}]},{"user":"KvaraMemories","text":"I don't want anybody writing the PSG final's score in advance.","replies":[{"user":"CurvaB","text":"I'M BUSY PAINTING A FOUR ON MY FRONT DOOR. PSG CAN WAIT.","replies":[{"user":"KvaraMemories","text":"That seems like a healthy way to spend today.","replies":[]}]},{"user":"ParisObserver","text":"Enjoy the celebration. We have our own nerves about the final.","replies":[]}]},{"user":"InterNorth","text":"From an Inter fan: this season's champion is legitimate. There is no dispute.","replies":[]},{"user":"MooreMagic","text":"Did Bellandi watch the pass for Beier? That's the football worth talking about.","replies":[{"user":"BeierHive","text":"Apparently he did","replies":[]}]},{"user":"PioNation","text":"Our striker has 45 goals now. I'll allow one day of unqualified happiness.","replies":[{"user":"PioHaterForNoReason","text":"One day of happiness is excessive.","replies":[{"user":"PioNation","text":"He has forty-five goals. There may never be a day you call enough.","replies":[]}]},{"user":"BeierHive","text":"Can the forwards be celebrated together for once, please?","replies":[]}]},{"user":"NapoliDoomer","text":"I can't switch from party mode to PSG nerves this quickly.","replies":[{"user":"NapoliTherapy","text":"Get some food into you before the European nerves begin.","replies":[{"user":"NapoliDoomer","text":"I ordered pasta but now I'm worrying the delivery driver supports Inter.","replies":[]}]},{"user":"OldSchoolNapoli","text":"The final will be there tomorrow. This evening won't happen twice.","replies":[]}]},{"user":"OldSchoolNapoli","text":"I still think his criticism after Udinese was too dramatic. A late equaliser didn't wipe out thirty-six matches of work.","replies":[]},{"user":"AzzurriSouth","text":"BELLANDI, GRAZIE. PLEASE DON'T RUIN IT TOMORROW.","replies":[{"user":"CurvaB","text":"I'LL ACCEPT HIS COMPLIMENT AND IGNORE THE BUT.","replies":[{"user":"AzzurriSouth","text":"IT'S BELLANDI. THERE IS ALWAYS A BUT.","replies":[]}]},{"user":"OldSchoolNapoli","text":"At least this one is about a real upcoming match rather than a manufactured dressing-room crisis.","replies":[]}]},{"user":"BuongiornoWall","text":"The clean sheet was the appropriate companion to the four goals.","replies":[{"user":"PeacockUnion","text":"Finally a sensible comment","replies":[]}]},{"user":"McTominayEngine","text":"Scott's goal being called an exclamation mark is fair.","replies":[]},{"user":"BeierHive","text":"Everyone praises Moore's pass. Beier still needed to turn it into a goal.","replies":[{"user":"MooreMagic","text":"Two artists, one moment","replies":[]}]},{"user":"ScudettoWatch","text":"87 points. Beyond Inter, beyond Roma. I wish Bellandi spent more time on that and less time treating PSG as if they're already on the pitch.","replies":[]},{"user":"RomaObserver","text":"The trophy is decided, but Milan still has football value.","replies":[{"user":"OldSchoolNapoli","text":"Champions should perform properly","replies":[]}]},{"user":"OliseAppreciation","text":"Please appreciate Olise while he's here. The season isn't finished.","replies":[]},{"user":"PazAppreciation","text":"A team can rotate without starting a scandal. Some pundits should remember that.","replies":[{"user":"TacticalNonno","text":"Indeed","replies":[]}]},{"user":"CurvaB","text":"I DEMAND ONE DAY WITHOUT EUROPEAN ANXIETY.","replies":[{"user":"ParisObserver","text":"We have a final to play too, you know.","replies":[{"user":"CurvaB","text":"AND I WILL THINK ABOUT IT AFTER DESSERT.","replies":[]}]},{"user":"NapoliDoomer","text":"It's the reminder that Paris is real that's doing me in.","replies":[]}]},{"user":"BergamoVisitor","text":"Napoli earned the title. Our cup final loss makes more sense watching this.","replies":[{"user":"OldSchoolNapoli","text":"Respect","replies":[]}]},{"user":"NapoliDoomer","text":"Possibility, not entitlement. My stomach is already doing gymnastics.","replies":[]},{"user":"PioHaterForNoReason","text":"I agree Paris is uncertain. What if Pio scores only twice?","replies":[{"user":"PioNation","text":"THAT WOULD BE LOVELY","replies":[]}]},{"user":"MooreMagic","text":"That early ball is why I believe we can compete with anyone.","replies":[]},{"user":"RossettiWatch","text":"How we use the Milan fixture should be a football question, not a moral test.","replies":[{"user":"OldSchoolNapoli","text":"Well put","replies":[]}]},{"user":"KvaraMemories","text":"2028 still matters, but it doesn't foretell 2031.","replies":[]},{"user":"TacticalNonno","text":"I'll give him credit for praising us properly. Still expect him to find fault if we rotate against Milan.","replies":[{"user":"OldSchoolNapoli","text":"A mature conclusion","replies":[]}]},{"user":"ScudettoWatch","text":"We can all dream of Paris, but somebody has to kick a ball on May 31. Tonight's trophy is already ours.","replies":[{"user":"PioNation","text":"For now, CHAMPIONS","replies":[]}]}]},{"id":"mikey-moore-fictional-title-night-interview-may19-2031","category":"Player Interview","date":"19 May 2031","byline":"Lorenzo Ferri · Player Interviews","headline":"THE PASS BEFORE THE RUN: MIKEY MOORE ON NAPOLI'S FOURTH STRAIGHT TITLE","dek":"In conversation with Lorenzo Ferri, Moore reflects on his header, two assists and the afternoon Napoli became champions again.","image":"assets/story-napoli-key-players-huddle.webp","imageCredit":"Season Room · Editorial illustration","longform":true,"body":["Napoli's fourth consecutive Scudetto was secured in a first half shaped by Mikey Moore: a header from Estêvão's cross, a pass for Pio Esposito and a through ball that sent Maximilian Beier in to score. The young winger spoke to Lorenzo Ferri about those decisions, his teammates and what comes next.","Ferri: A header from an Estêvão cross. Is that how you expected your afternoon to begin?","Moore: Not really, but I'll take it. People think you need to make a complicated move to score a good goal. Sometimes you just get into the right place.","Ferri: You then created the second for Pio. How do you decide when to shoot and when to pass?","Moore: You look for the better option. Pio's a brilliant finisher. I want him to have those chances. And he's the first one to try to put somebody else through when he can.","Ferri: The pass to Beier before the run was fully visible looked almost impossible to plan.","Moore: You see a little gap. You know the way Maxi runs. If you wait until he's completely through, the gap's gone. I'm just glad he finished it so well.","Ferri: Your figures are now ten goals and thirteen assists this season. Which matters more?","Moore: Whatever helped us win. Goals are brilliant. Passing to someone who scores is brilliant. I don't want a defender to know which I'm thinking about.","Ferri: Is it difficult learning alongside forwards with Pio's and Beier's numbers?","Moore: Sometimes you wonder if you're doing enough. Then you see how much they work and you understand what the standard is. You learn, you try things, you keep going.","Ferri: Scott McTominay scored the fourth. Does that make this feel like a team achievement rather than your individual performance?","Moore: Of course. Estêvão found me, I found Pio and Maxi, Pio found Scott. That's the game, isn't it? Everybody helps somebody.","Ferri: Four straight Scudetti. Can you take that in?","Moore: Not properly yet. You know what the older lads have been through to win them. You don't want to waste a moment like this.","Ferri: AC Milan is next and then PSG in a European final. How do you avoid thinking ahead?","Moore: We can think about those tomorrow. Today we won the league. You have to give yourself the chance to enjoy it.","Ferri: The headed goal or the pass to Beier? You have to choose.","Moore: No chance. Ask Maxi. He'll probably say his finish was better than both."],"comments":[{"user":"MooreMagic","text":"His answer about the goal or the pass is perfect. Beier will be unbearable if somebody shows him that last line.","replies":[{"user":"BeierHive","text":"He wouldn't be wrong to say that. The finish was lovely.","replies":[{"user":"MooreMagic","text":"Without the pass he gets to finish precisely nothing.","replies":[]}]},{"user":"TacticalNonno","text":"The fact we can argue about which half of one move was better tells you everything.","replies":[]}]},{"user":"CurvaB","text":"HE'S TOO MODEST. I WILL CELEBRATE LOUDLY FOR HIM.","replies":[{"user":"NapoliTherapy","text":"You've been celebrating for about sixteen hours straight.","replies":[{"user":"CurvaB","text":"AND I HAVE ONLY JUST STARTED.","replies":[]}]}]},{"user":"PioNation","text":"The way he talks about finding Pio instead of shooting is what I love. Pio would do the same for him.","replies":[{"user":"MooreMagic","text":"Everyone's obsessed with the Beier ball. The Pio assist was the first proof he could take the match over.","replies":[{"user":"PioNation","text":"And Pio made his chance count. That's how you win a title.","replies":[]}]},{"user":"McTominayEngine","text":"Pio then gives Scott his chance. Everybody passing the gift along.","replies":[]}]},{"user":"TacticalNonno","text":"That answer about the gap closing explains the third goal better than all the replays I've watched.","replies":[{"user":"BeierHive","text":"Because Beier is already moving while the pass is being chosen.","replies":[{"user":"TacticalNonno","text":"That understanding takes work; it isn't just a moment of improvisation.","replies":[]}]}]},{"user":"NapoliDoomer","text":"The answer about sometimes wondering if he's doing enough hit unexpectedly hard.","replies":[{"user":"NapoliTherapy","text":"At that age, being surrounded by guys scoring forty goals must be both brilliant and terrifying.","replies":[{"user":"NapoliDoomer","text":"And he still played his own game in a title decider.","replies":[]}]}]},{"user":"EstevaoElectric","text":"I'm just pleased the opening cross gets its rightful mention.","replies":[]},{"user":"BeierHive","text":"Beier is going to tell everybody his finish was the difficult part. I'd love to hear Moore argue back.","replies":[{"user":"MooreMagic","text":"I'd let him boast about it if I could have watched those two laughing at the final whistle.","replies":[{"user":"BeierHive","text":"Careful. You're inventing a conversation now.","replies":[]}]}]},{"user":"SaladinoOutNow","text":"Still nobody asking the important question: why didn't we win this game seven nil?","replies":[{"user":"CurvaB","text":"BECAUSE FOUR WAS MORE THAN ENOUGH TO CLAIM THE SCUDETTO.","replies":[{"user":"SaladinoOutNow","text":"That word 'enough' is exactly what worries me.","replies":[]}]},{"user":"MooreMagic","text":"If Moore found three more runs you would complain he didn't find four.","replies":[]}]},{"user":"McTominayEngine","text":"He didn't forget Scott's goal. Proper recognition.","replies":[{"user":"StachAppreciation","text":"A fourth from a midfielder was a good reminder that the scoreline belongs to the team.","replies":[{"user":"McTominayEngine","text":"And that our Scott never stops arriving.","replies":[]}]}]},{"user":"RossettiWatch","text":"I liked that he talks about learning even while the team keeps winning. That's a good mindset.","replies":[{"user":"OldSchoolNapoli","text":"The best young ones realise they're still students. The dangerous ones decide they've learned it all.","replies":[{"user":"RossettiWatch","text":"Exactly. I hope everyone in the squad takes that part to heart.","replies":[]}]}]},{"user":"AzzurriSouth","text":"GIOVANE, BRAVO, CORAGGIOSO.","replies":[]},{"user":"NapoliTherapy","text":"We get an interview and a trophy. Not a bad day.","replies":[{"user":"NapoliDoomer","text":"I can't imagine living through these matches without the reaction afterwards.","replies":[{"user":"NapoliTherapy","text":"Then maybe you should stop expecting disaster after three nil.","replies":[]}]}]},{"user":"BuongiornoWall","text":"The teamwork point is more useful than any boastful declaration.","replies":[]},{"user":"InterNorth","text":"It must be quite something to be a youngster in a team on its fourth title.","replies":[]},{"user":"MooreMagic","text":"He sounds confident but he doesn't pretend all of this pressure is easy. I respect that.","replies":[]},{"user":"PioHaterForNoReason","text":"He should have asked why Pio didn't assist the opening goal.","replies":[{"user":"PioNation","text":"Because Estêvão supplied the opening cross. An excellent pass, in fact.","replies":[{"user":"PioHaterForNoReason","text":"Conveniently, I see every winger conspiring against my evidence.","replies":[]}]}]},{"user":"NapoliDoomer","text":"All this joy and Paris is still to come. What an exhausting club.","replies":[]},{"user":"StachAppreciation","text":"You still need the runners and finishers for an assist to mean anything.","replies":[]},{"user":"CurvaB","text":"NEXT INTERVIEW: ASK THE BALL HOW IT KNEW WHERE BEIER WOULD BE.","replies":[{"user":"TacticalNonno","text":"We could put a microphone in the grass where the pass arrived.","replies":[{"user":"CurvaB","text":"GOOD. THE GRASS IS OUR NEXT NATIONAL TREASURE.","replies":[]}]}]},{"user":"NapoliTherapy","text":"This is the right way to think about it. Celebrate the Scudetto now; Paris gets its own day.","replies":[]},{"user":"AzzurriSouth","text":"QUATTRO SCUDETTI. MAMMA MIA.","replies":[]}]}];const ids=new Set(incoming.map(a=>a.id));D.articles=[...incoming,...(D.articles||[]).filter(a=>!ids.has(a.id))];})();
